    <briefdescription>
<para>An opaque object representing a hash code. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This object represents the result of hashing some entity. It is intended to be used to implement hashtables or other hashing-based data structures. While it wraps and exposes a numeric value, this value should not be trusted to be stable or predictable across processes or executions.</para>
<para>In order to obtain the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1hash__code" kindref="compound">hash_code</ref> for an object &apos;x&apos;: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keyword">using<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespacellvm_1a0e2e479cf4860dc8a00614e36ee3d5e9" kindref="member">llvm::hash_value</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">llvm::hash_code<sp/>code<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="classllvm_1_1hash__code_1a3bae3ed52c5efcdd61eea5789ba14a9c" kindref="member">hash_value</ref>(x);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
